---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro'

const media = (name: string) => `/blog/2026-11-reader-0.3.0/${name}`
const badge = '/blog/2026-10-ios-testflight/testflight-badge.png'
const testflight = 'https://testflight.apple.com/join/JrHyntNU'
---
<BaseLayout
  article={{ published: '2026-11-22' }}
  title="Tome Reader 0.3.0: iPad and offline reading — Tome"
  description="Tome Reader 0.3.0 is on TestFlight with a real iPad layout and a library that works without a connection."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main>
  <article class="blog-article">
    <header class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-32 pb-12 text-center">
      <div class="accent-glow"></div>
      <a href="/blog" class="blog-back">&larr; Blog</a>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4 leading-[1.1]">
        Tome Reader 0.3.0: iPad and offline reading
      </h1>
      <div class="blog-meta">
        <time class="blog-date" datetime="2026-11-22">2026-11-22</time>
        <span class="blog-date">&middot;</span>
        <span class="blog-date">2 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="blog-body">

      <p>
        The last post ended its list of known limits with "iPhone only. No iPad layout yet." That
        was the most asked-for thing since, so Tome Reader 0.3.0 is mostly that, plus the other
        thing a reading app should do: work when the server is out of reach. It is on TestFlight
        now; the beta stays free through the end of 2026.
      </p>

      <p class="blog-badge">
        <a href={testflight}><img src={badge} alt="Available on TestFlight" height="60" /></a>
      </p>

      <p>
        Every picture and clip below is the sample library built into the app, which now includes
        two episodes of the webcomic Pepper&amp;Carrot. No server at hand? "Try a sample library"
        on the first screen gets you the same.
      </p>

      <div class="blog-clip">
        <video controls muted playsinline preload="none" poster={media('clip-home-fan-poster.jpg')} width="1600" height="1044" aria-label="The cover fan on Home on iPad">
          <source src={media('clip-home-fan.mp4')} type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      </div>
      <p class="blog-caption">Home on an iPad.</p>


      <!-- ── PAGE CURL ── -->

      <h2 id="page-curl">Page curl</h2>

      <div class="blog-clip">
        <video controls muted playsinline preload="none" poster={media('clip-page-curl-poster.jpg')} width="1600" height="1044" aria-label="Turning comic pages with a curl on iPad">
          <source src={media('clip-page-curl.mp4')} type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      </div>

      <ul>
        <li>Pages turn with a curl in EPUB books and comics. It is the default on iPad and a setting on iPhone.</li>
        <li>Sideways, a comic shows two pages at a time.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- ── IPAD ── -->

      <h2 id="ipad">iPad</h2>

      <div class="blog-clip">
        <video controls muted playsinline preload="none" poster={media('clip-series-split-poster.jpg')} width="1600" height="1044" aria-label="The Series tab on iPad, list and series side by side">
          <source src={media('clip-series-split.mp4')} type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      </div>

      <ul>
        <li>The app fills the iPad screen in both orientations instead of running as a stretched phone app.</li>
        <li>Turned sideways, the Series tab shows the list and the series you picked side by side.</li>
        <li>Stats uses the wider screen, and the reader's column width and text size are set for large screens.</li>
        <li>Home shows the cover fan or a banner; the choice is in Settings.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- ── OFFLINE ── -->

      <h2 id="offline">Offline</h2>

      <div class="blog-shot blog-shot-row">
        <img src={media('04-offline-library.webp')} alt="The Library without a connection, with the number of books on the device" width="368" height="800" loading="lazy" />
        <img src={media('07-downloads-on-phone.webp')} alt="Settings listing the downloaded books with their sizes" width="368" height="800" loading="lazy" />
      </div>

      <ul>
        <li>The library is kept on the device in the background. Library, Series, book pages, Home and Stats open without a connection.</li>
        <li>The Library says how many books are on the device, and Settings lists them with their sizes.</li>
        <li>What you read offline is kept and sent when the server is reachable again. If you read further on another device in the meantime, the newer position wins.</li>
        <li>A whole series can be downloaded at once, and downloads wait for a connection instead of failing.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- ── SERIES ZOOM ── -->

      <h2 id="series-zoom">Series open from their cover</h2>

      <div class="blog-clip blog-clip-upright">
        <video controls muted playsinline preload="none" poster={media('clip-series-zoom-poster.jpg')} width="1044" height="1600" aria-label="A series zooming out of its cover">
          <source src={media('clip-series-zoom.mp4')} type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      </div>

      <p>
        Tapping a series in the Library or the Series tab zooms it out of its cover, and closing
        it zooms back in.
      </p>

      <!-- ── WIDGETS ── -->

      <h2 id="widgets">Widgets</h2>

      <div class="blog-shot blog-shot-single"><img src={media('05-widgets.webp')} alt="Tome widgets on the Home Screen" width="368" height="800" loading="lazy" /></div>

      <ul>
        <li>Home Screen widgets in every size, including the extra-large one on iPad: continue reading, the week, streak, today and what is in rotation.</li>
        <li>Lock Screen widgets for the current book and the streak.</li>
        <li>They follow the theme you picked in the app.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- ── ALSO NEW ── -->

      <h2 id="also-new">Also new</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>The book page shows your progress first for a book you are reading and the description first for one you have not started.</li>
        <li>New Stats pages, with Tome 3.1.0 or later on the server.</li>
        <li>The sample library has a comic: "The Potion Contest" and "The Magic Contest" from Pepper&amp;Carrot.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- ── KNOWN LIMITS ── -->

      <h2 id="known-limits">Known limits</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>On 13-inch iPads a few pages do not use the full width yet.</li>
        <li>Widgets follow the app's theme, not the system's light and dark setting.</li>
        <li>You need your own Tome server, or the sample library. TestFlight builds expire after 90 days; new builds replace them before that.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- ── FEEDBACK ── -->

      <h2 id="feedback">Feedback</h2>

      <p>
        Bugs, ideas and questions go to the <a href="https://github.com/bndct-devops/tome/discussions/categories/tome-reader-ios">Tome Reader (iOS)</a> category
        in GitHub Discussions; Settings in the app has a link to it. If you would rather not
        post publicly, mail <a href="mailto:tome@bndct.dev">tome@bndct.dev</a>. Please mention the
        version and build number from Settings &rsaquo; About.
      </p>

      <p class="blog-badge">
        <a href={testflight}><img src={badge} alt="Available on TestFlight" height="60" /></a>
      </p>

      <p class="blog-credit">
        Pepper&amp;Carrot by David Revoy, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>, from <a href="https://www.peppercarrot.com">www.peppercarrot.com</a>. Pages resized. David Revoy is not affiliated with Tome and does not endorse it.
      </p>

      <div class="blog-footer-links">
        <a href={testflight}>Join the beta</a>
        <a href="/why">Why Tome?</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/bndct-devops/tome">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .blog-back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .blog-back:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .blog-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .blog-date {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  }
  .blog-body {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px 80px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .blog-body p {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .blog-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: 56px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .blog-body h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 32px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .blog-body a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent-soft);
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    transition: text-decoration-color 0.15s;
  }
  .blog-body a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .blog-body ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5em;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .blog-body li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .blog-body li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .blog-body code {
    font-size: 0.85em;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .blog-body em {
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .blog-shot {
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  .blog-caption {
    font-size: 0.82rem !important;
    color: var(--muted) !important;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: -8px !important;
    margin-bottom: 32px !important;
  }
  .blog-shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .blog-shot-single {
    max-width: 320px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }
  .blog-badge {
    text-align: center;
    margin: 28px 0 !important;
  }
  .blog-badge img {
    display: inline-block;
    height: 60px;
    width: auto;
  }
  .blog-body .blog-badge a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .blog-footer-links {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .blog-shot-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .blog-clip {
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  .blog-clip video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--card);
  }
  .blog-clip-upright {
    max-width: 320px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }
  .blog-credit {
    font-size: 0.82rem !important;
    color: var(--muted) !important;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .blog-credit + .blog-footer-links {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .blog-body h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; }
  }
</style>
